      "math_academy_id": "q-164332",
      "sequence_position": 12,
      "problem": "The table below gives the values of ${Φ}^{-1}(p)$ for different values of $p,$ where $p=Φ(z)$ is the cumulative distribution function for the standard normal distribution. Find the value of $z$ such that $P(Z\\le z)=0.10.$\n\n| $p$ | $\\,0.900\\,$ | $\\,0.950\\,$ | $\\,0.975\\,$ | $\\,0.990\\,$ | $\\,0.995\\,$ | $\\,0.999\\,$ | $\\,0.9995\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${Φ}^{-1}(p)$ | $\\,1.2816\\,$ | $\\,1.6449\\,$ | $\\,1.9600\\,$ | $\\,2.3263\\,$ | $\\,2.5758\\,$ | $\\,3.0902\\,$ | $\\,3.2905\\,$ |",
      "worked_solution": "From the table, notice that\n\n$$\nP(Z\\le 1.2816)=0.90.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nP(Z\\ge 1.2816)=1-0.90=0.10.\n$$\n\nBy the symmetry of the standard normal distribution, we have\n\n$$\nΦ(-1.2816)=0.10.\n$$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14165008/assets/feb06180815c7ae83a5034ff8933700fd5778c9ab0bfba54fe95bb67104662b7.png)\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Φ(-1.2816) & =0.10 \\\\ P(Z\\le -1.2816) & =0.10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required value of $z$ is $-1.2816.$",
